The public function `render_annotations(entries)` accepts an iterable of three-element sequences `(name, type_name, description)`. Every element must be a nonempty string after stripping. Names must be unique after stripping. Return a newly allocated list of strings formatted as `name [type_name]: description`, ordered by stripped name in ascending case-sensitive order. Empty input returns `[]`. Raise `ValueError` for malformed entries or duplicates. Do not mutate or alias caller-owned containers.

Known-bad source:
```python
def render_annotations(entries):
    try:
        source = list(entries)
    except TypeError as exc:
        raise ValueError("entries must be iterable") from exc

    normalized = []
    names = set()
    for entry in source:
        if isinstance(entry, (str, bytes)):
            raise ValueError("entry must have three fields")
        try:
            parts = list(entry)
        except TypeError as exc:
            raise ValueError("entry must be iterable") from exc
        if len(parts) != 3 or any(not isinstance(value, str) for value in parts):
            raise ValueError("entry must contain three strings")
        name, type_name, description = (value.strip() for value in parts)
        if not name or not type_name or not description:
            raise ValueError("fields must be nonempty")
        if name in names:
            raise ValueError("duplicate name")
        names.add(name)
        normalized.append((name, type_name, description))

    normalized.sort(key=lambda item: item[0], reverse=True)
    return [f"{name} [{type_name}]: {description}" for name, type_name, description in normalized]
```

